{
  "id": "Compound::DB00490 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Buspirone is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular interactions involving prochlorperazine and domperidone, both of which bind to the Cyp3a4 enzyme. The evidence suggests that Buspirone may influence the expression or activity of Cyp3a4 via the activation of Dystonic Reaction or Cogwheel Rigidity, which are both mediated by prochlorperazine or domperidone. These conditions, in turn, trigger binding to Cyp3a4, indicating a potential role in modulating enzyme activity. The shared pathway through the N-Alkylpiperazine class and the Agent Affecting Nervous System category further supports a common mechanism of action. While the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear, the cumulative evidence points to a possible regulatory relationship between Buspirone and Cyp3a4, likely through the activation of downstream pathways involving prochlorperazine or domperidone.",
